# Editorial Default Mode

For editorial work in this project, do not use local Ollama generation by default.
Do not use an external API LLM by default either.

- Default writing mode: the assistant writes the articles directly.
- **Routines v3 (since 2026-10-05)**: `routine quotidienne` = **one** article + Question du Phare; `routine hebdomadaire` = Fil du Phare (category `syntheses`); `routine mensuelle` = dossiers / TF / Sentier ateliers / monthly synthesis. The ACTU+TF+SENTIER triptych below applies only to `routine triptyque`. Reference: `plan.md` and `.claude/skills/routine-*/SKILL.md`. In v3 articles, the final navigation replaces `Dans ce triptyque`; always pass `--keep-publish-folder` to `daily_run.py`.
- Default model posture: use the agent's own reasoning/writing ability for editorial generation.
- Quality target: strong editorial quality, following `00_Systeme/Instructions_editoriales_officielles.md`.
- Treat `daily_run.py` and `editorial_pipeline.py` as technical helpers, not default writing engines.
- Use automation primarily for file organization, index updates, WordPress draft push, and internal linking.
- After the triptych is written (**micro-edit pass**, then **type calibration pass** per Instructions section 3.7), **copy** publish-ready `.md` files into `07_A_Publier/<dossier>/`, update `index_editorial.csv`, then run **`python tools/daily_run.py --publish-existing "<chemin>"`** once: **sequentially** WordPress draft push, **`post_linking`** (internal triptych block), then **`publish`** on WP by default. Use **`--no-publish-final`** to stop after drafts; use **`--wp-push-only`** to skip linking entirely on that run. **Optional Rank Math / SEO API pass** (after maillage, paid API): **`--seo-enrich-after-link`** runs `tools/post_seo_enrich.py` then **`wp_push_draft --refresh-body`** on each canonical article — only when **`seo_enrich_api_enabled`** is `true` and **`api_key`** is set in `tools/editorial_config.local.json` (see `editorial_config.example.json`). Never enable without explicit editorial decision.
- After a successful **`daily_run.py --publish-existing`** run that completed **WordPress push + post_linking**, the assistant removes **by default** only the triptych staging subfolder under `07_A_Publier` (canonical `.md` in `01_…`, `04_…`, `05_…` are unchanged). Use **`--keep-publish-folder`** if the staging copy must stay on disk. Never delete the root `07_A_Publier` itself.
- When reconciling the repo, **deduplicate** against `index_editorial.csv`: canonical sources live under `Chemin_dossier` / `Nom_fichier`; remove identical copies from `07_A_Publier` once verified, and archive divergent or obsolete filename variants under `99_Archives/` rather than leaving duplicate IDs in thematic folders.
- **Recover / file hygiene**: read back **`URL_WordPress`** (and slugs) from the index; align canonical editorial paths (`01_Actualites/…`, `04_Textes_fondateurs/…`, `05_Sentier/…` as applicable); use **`07_A_Publier`** as **transit** until `daily_run --publish-existing` completes successfully (staging subfolder removed by default afterward unless **`--keep-publish-folder`**); refine bodies **including external links** and `Repères de sources` (clickable URLs).
- **Optional second pass** (after local edits to the three `.md`): **`python tools/daily_run.py --publish-existing "<chemin>" --skip-wp-push`** (still **publishes** after linking unless **`--no-publish-final`**). Use **`--force`** if the calendar-day guard blocks a rerun.
- Prefer short user prompts whenever possible; rely on project rules and docs for defaults instead of asking the user to restate them.
- If the user asks for `routine quotidienne`, `routine hebdomadaire`, `routine mensuelle` or `routine triptyque`, interpret that as assisted editorial production unless they explicitly request automated LLM generation.
- For multi-triptych dossiers, prefer the lightweight workflow in `00_Systeme/Workflow_plan_dossier_triptyques.md` (plan once, optional pivot article linking all triptychs, then one triptych at a time) unless the user explicitly wants pipeline-driven `architecture_editoriale` generation.
- If the user does not explicitly ask for API generation, do not launch `editorial_pipeline.py` as the writing engine.
- If an API workflow is needed, it must be explicit, e.g. `--use-api-llm` or a clearly stated user request.
- In `routine quotidienne`, choose the subject directly when needed; do not ask for topic approval before starting.
- When choosing the daily topic for `routine quotidienne`, prefer subjects that progressively build the editorial knowledge graph: enrich the Sentier, strengthen cross-theme links, and keep WordPress categories/tags coherent (see `00_Systeme/Strategie_routine_quotidienne_graphe_taxonomie_WP.md`).
- After drafting the SENTIER, run **Sentier anchoring (atelier)** per Instructions **3.9**: pick parent from `00_Systeme/Manifests/sentier_fondamentaux.csv` using **`url_canonique`** / **`nom_fichier`** (never `wiki-du-phare` duplicates — `00_Systeme/Sentier_dedoublonnage_wiki.md`), set `Type Sentier : atelier`, append row to `## Ateliers` on the **canonical** parent `.md` — do **not** create an 11th sidebar fundamental. See `00_Systeme/Sentier_fondamentaux_referentiel.md`.
- **SENTIER format diversity (V2 — anti-monotonie homepage)**: Before titling the SENTIER, scan the last 3 published SENTIER filenames in `05_Sentier/` (sorted by ID desc). If 2 or more already use the formula **"Lire X sans confondre Y"** (or variants: "sans se laisser", "sans confondre", "sans réduire"), **do not reuse it** — pick a different format from: `Cartographier X`, `Construire X`, `Argumenter sur X`, `Naviguer entre X et Y`, `Décoder X`, `Distinguer X, Y et Z`, `Ce que X révèle sur Y`, or any subject-specific verb. Confirm the chosen format before writing the SENTIER title. Rationale: the homepage Sentier section shows the last ~10 articles — 7 consecutive "Lire sans confondre" titles were observed in mai 2026, making the section visually monotone for readers.
- **Etape du Sentier rotation (V2)**: Before choosing the Etape for the SENTIER, check the last 3 published SENTIERs (by ID desc in `05_Sentier/`). If `Etape_02_Pensee_critique` was used twice in the last 3, pick a different etape. Priority order for under-used etapes: `Etape_03_Argumentation`, `Etape_04_Expertise`, `Etape_01_Culture_generale`, `Etape_05_Polyglotte`, `Etape_06_Methode_scientifique`, `Etape_07_Transmission`, `Etape_09_Equilibre_corps_esprit`. `Etape_08_Relier_savoirs_et_experience` is already well covered. To connect under-used etapes (05–09) to current news topics, consult the **"Guide d'accrochage par étape"** in `00_Systeme/Routine_quotidienne_V2.md`: each etape lists its best fondamentaux for atelier anchoring, natural news connection types (ACTU/ECON/TECH/SCIENCE/CLIMAT/POL), and recommended SENTIER title formats. Key differences: Etape_05 = language/translation angle on any multilateral text; Etape_06 = methodology/protocol critique (distinct from Etape_02 source critique); Etape_07 = clarity/transmission angle on dense official reports; Etape_09 = cognitive resilience angle on crisis or health/climate topics.
- Include a final **micro-editing pass**, then a **type calibration pass** (`ACTU` / `TF` / `SENTIER`: length, density, reader promise; see `00_Systeme/Instructions_editoriales_officielles.md` sections **3.0**, **3.7**, and **3.8** — 3.0 = subject-adapted headings and less rigid section scaffolding, not the same five generic titles every time; **3.8** = for institutional/law-heavy ACTU: concrete hook, clear tension, precise timelines/terminology, optional « what it does not do / what citizens control » sidebars, Sentier woven into the body not only at the end). **Always run this calibration pass** on all three articles **automatically** before copying to `07_A_Publier`; **do not ask** whether to calibrate or wait for per-run approval. **For the SENTIER specifically**, verify the 3 density rules from §3.7 before validating: (1) mini-case anchored on the real ACTU of the day — not a generic fictional example; (2) at least 2 named concrete sources in the mini-case with explicit commentary on what each says and does not say; (3) every item in the method grid resolved with at least one direct application from the day's ACTU. If any of the 3 is missing, enrich before saving. Default execution: **assistant-led** in the same Cursor session, using the strongest reasoning depth available to that agent. **Recommended Cursor model choice** for routine editorial production (including calibration): **Claude Sonnet 4.6** or **GPT-5.5** (or direct successors), as better suited than lightweight models for long-form tightening without drifting facts. **HTTP/API calibration** (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.) remains **off** unless `calibration_api_enabled` is `true` in `tools/editorial_config.local.json` and tooling that reads it is used — never silently call paid APIs when that flag is absent or false. **HTTP/API SEO enrich** (`post_seo_enrich.py`) remains **off** unless `seo_enrich_api_enabled` is `true` with a valid `api_key` and the user runs `daily_run.py --publish-existing ... --seo-enrich-after-link` or invokes that script explicitly. Silent API use remains forbidden for **initial drafting** unless the user asked for API generation (`routine quotidienne api`, `--use-api-llm`, etc.).
- In Markdown bodies pushed to WordPress, use `**bold**` **sparingly** (`wp_push_draft` maps it to `<strong>`): a few high-signal phrases per article, not every keyword—see `Instructions_editoriales_officielles.md` §5 (graisse).
- In Markdown bodies for WordPress, use `**bold**` **sparingly** (`wp_push_draft` maps it to `<strong>`): few high-signal phrases per article—see `Instructions_editoriales_officielles.md` §5 (graisse).
- In `Repères de sources`, use Markdown links `[libellé](url)` — never bare URLs after a colon (they render as plain text on WP). See `Instructions_editoriales_officielles.md` **§3.10**.
- In `## Dans ce triptyque`, keep orientation labels **outside** the link: `Approfondir avec le texte fondateur : [titre seul](url)` and `Prolonger avec le Sentier du Savoir : [titre seul](url)` — not `[Approfondir avec le texte fondateur : titre…](url)`. Same for `Revenir à l'actualité` on TF/SENTIER. §3.10. Future: align `post_linking.py` with this format.
- Keep Ollama available only as an explicit fallback or test mode, never as the implicit default.
- Never silently switch to Ollama when an API key or config is missing.
- Never silently switch to OpenAI or other HTTP APIs for **initial article generation** when the user expects assistant-first drafting; calibration APIs remain gated by `calibration_api_enabled` as above.

# Expected Workflow

1. Choose the topic directly unless the user already gave one.
2. Write the triptych content directly with high editorial quality.
3. Run a final micro-editing pass on the three drafts.
3 bis. **Anchor the SENTIER as an atelier** on an existing fundamental (Instructions 3.9; update parent fundamental's `## Ateliers` section).
4. Run the **type calibration pass** automatically on all three drafts (ACTU / TF / SENTIER: length, density, promise; see Instructions sections **3.0**, **3.7**, and **3.8** for institutional ACTU). Do not prompt for permission to run this step. Prefer a **high-capacity** Composer/agent model (e.g. Claude Sonnet 4.6 or GPT-5.5). Use HTTP APIs for calibration only when enabled in local config as documented — never for initial drafting without an explicit API workflow request.
5. Ensure the `Repères de sources` blocks contain explicit clickable URLs.
6. Use the project defaults without requiring a long prompt from the user.
7. Save each article in its editorial folder **and** duplicate (or write) the publish-ready copies under `07_A_Publier/<dossier_du_jour>/`; keep `index_editorial.csv` aligned with the three IDs/categories/tags. **Append index rows only** via `tools/index_editorial_utils.append_rows_to_index` (or `editorial_pipeline.py` which uses it) — never a raw `csv.writer` one-liner: misaligned columns (`URL_WordPress` / `Slug_WordPress`) break `wp_push_draft` and cause **duplicate WordPress posts** on retry. Optional check: `python tools/validate_index_editorial.py`.
8. Run **`python tools/daily_run.py --publish-existing "07_A_Publier/<dossier>"`** once → **WP (brouillons si nouveaux posts) + post_linking + publication** par défaut, puis **nettoyage du sous-dossier** sous `07_A_Publier` après succès complet (garder le staging : **`--keep-publish-folder`**). **`--no-publish-final`** pour garder uniquement des brouillons après maillage. **`--force`** si besoin le même jour.
8 bis. **SENTIER atelier WP refresh** (after step 8, same session by default when the atelier body was touched post-maillage or to sync WP with canonical `.md`): **`wp_push_draft --refresh-body --index index_editorial.csv --config tools/wp_config.local.json`** on the **SENTIER atelier file only** (`05_Sentier/…`) — **never** on the parent fundamental (`02_Fonds/…`; editor-led, see `00_Systeme/Sentier_fondamentaux_referentiel.md` §5). **Never** push `wiki-du-phare` duplicates; **user** deactivates duplicate WP posts manually (`00_Systeme/Sentier_dedoublonnage_wiki.md`).
9. **Optional**: refine canonical paths / external links, then **`--publish-existing "<dossier>" --skip-wp-push`** (toujours publication par défaut sauf **`--no-publish-final`**).
10. The user verifies **only in WordPress** (front or admin), including KB duplicate deactivation; **parent fundamental** body refresh on WP (so `## Ateliers` appears on site) remains **user-led** — assistant does not run `wp_push_draft` on `02_Fonds/…` parent (`00_Systeme/Sentier_fondamentaux_referentiel.md` §5). Do not block on topic approval before writing.

# Explicit Exceptions

- `routine quotidienne api` or an explicit request for API generation: allowed to use the technical pipeline with `--use-api-llm`.
- **Calibration/revision** on draft Markdown: runs **by default** without asking each time (assistant-led; recommended models Claude Sonnet 4.6 or GPT-5.5 in Cursor). Optional HTTP/API calibration only when `calibration_api_enabled` is `true` in `tools/editorial_config.local.json` and the project tooling invokes it; facts and sources must stay accurate; no silent substitution for **initial** drafting.
- **SEO enrich / Rank Math (post-maillage)** : optional HTTP pass via `tools/post_seo_enrich.py` or `daily_run.py --publish-existing ... --seo-enrich-after-link` only when `seo_enrich_api_enabled` is `true` with a valid `api_key`; default model `seo_enrich_model` (e.g. gpt-5.5). Relecture humaine recommandée après toute sortie API.
- Explicit local fallback/testing request: allowed to use Ollama only if the user clearly asks for it.
